====Celestial Destruction====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Celestial Destruction
|moveId=kenshiro_214a,kenshiro_214c,kenshiro_214c_6c,kenshiro_214ac,kenshiro_214ac_6c
|input=214A/C/AC
|input2=qcb+A/C/AC
|description5=Kenshiro performs a short-ranged ki blast. 
* All versions leave the opponent standing on hit
* The heavy and REV versions have an optional follow-up attack that is performed with 6P. It knocks the opponent down on hit
* Despite Kenshiro using channeled ki to perform it, it’s still a strike and can be countered/parried as usual
----
'''Light version (214A)''': A safe ender that’s optimal for damage from light confirms
* A very straightforward striking special
* Combos from Kenshiro’s lights
* On Counter Hit or Wild Punish, links to far A
* Does more damage than 236B, but leaves Kenshiro further away on hit
----
'''Heavy version (214C)''': Kenshiro’s plus-on-block special move
* +2 on block while being barely fast enough to combo from heavies
* Both the first hit and the follow-up launch on Counter Hit
* Links to 5AC on Wild Punish
* Not very combo-friendly due to its startup
* You can confirm the follow-up attack easily when you see the first part hit
----
'''REV version (214AC)''': The version most commonly used in combos
* Similar to the heavy version, but is MUCH faster to start up, letting you cancel heavies into it to start combos
* Both the first hit and the optional follow-up attack have REV Accel properties
* Kenshiro’s only plus-on-block REV special. Use REV Accel into this on block to keep your offense going

'''Debuff Trigger''': The debuff is applied and triggered by the follow-up attack. When it does so, the knockback is slightly higher, improving Kenshiro’s REV Accel routes and combo conversions. That said, the first hit avoiding the debuff trigger is situationally useful to either keep the debuff on the opponent or to save the trigger for later in the combo.
